    {
      "title": "Shopify's Catalog Mapping feature is fake?",
      "url": "https://www.reddit.com/r/shopify/comments/1wcn6q4/shopifys_catalog_mapping_feature_is_fake/",
      "source": "r/shopify",
      "published": "2026-09-10T15:56:36+00:00",
      "summary": "In their Agentic Dashboard sales channel, you can remap what Shopify Catalog sends to AI shopping assistants like ChatGPT. Instead of your product description it can pull from a metafield. The thinking is you replace the normal human-focused product description with an alternate description for AI agents stored in a metafield. I've done this on two stores, at the end of August... and no result. It does nothing. Every day I check the catalog record through the UCP API. 14 days later, still nothin",
